  "description": "T1 London Plane (Platanus × acerifolia)Carry out cyclical crown management works to the mature London Plane by removing all recent extension growth and reducing back to theprevious established reduction points. Works to include the selective removal of approximately 2-3 metres of new growth throughout thecanopy, reinstating the tree to its previous management profile whilst maintaining a balanced and uniform crown structure.T2 - MagnoliaCarry out a sensitive crown prune and reshape, selectively removing excessive, crossing or unbalanced growth whilst retaining the tree'snatural form and amenity value.T3 - Lime TreePrune back overhanging lateral growth to the boundary wall line and undertake a crown lift to provide approximately 5 metres clearance abovestreet level, removing growth encroaching onto the public highway and associated infrastructure.T4 - Weeping WillowPrune back overhanging growth to the boundary wall line, maintaining a balanced canopy whilst reducing encroachment beyond the propertyboundary.T5 - EucalyptusPollard tree back to suitable historic reduction points in order to maintain size and manage future growth.&nbsp;All works will be carried out in compliance with BS 39982010 - Tree Work Recommendations, adhering to current industry best practice.Reason for works:&nbsp;General tree maintenance and light starvation to property",
